# Logic Model Extractor — Project Context

## What this app does
Web app that reliably extracts structured logic models from uploaded documents (PDF, DOCX, PPTX)
using Gemini vision/text for downstream processing, lets users edit/verify results, and exports
CSV for coding. Document-quality/causal-chain critique is out of scope — see
`docs/specs/scope-extraction-only-2026-09.md`.

## Tech stack (Golden Path)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Frontend:** React 19 + Vite (port 3000) + Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`)
- **API:** Express (`server.ts`) on port 3011 — Gemini key stays server-side only
- **AI:** Google Gemini via `@google/genai` in `server/geminiLogicModel.ts` (extract) and
  `server/geminiLogicModelGroups.ts` (multi-logic-model detect pre-pass)
- **File handling:** npm packages (`pdfjs-dist`, `mammoth`, `docx-preview`, `html2canvas`, `jszip`, `turndown`, `jspdf`)
- **Export:** CSV download + PDF generation (`pdfService`)
- **Brand:** `config/brand.ts` (SDP defaults)
- **Production:** `npm start` builds client and serves `dist` + API from Express

## Key directories
- `App.tsx` — upload queue, extract → edit flow, CSV/PDF export
- `components/` — FileUpload, LogicModelEditor, LogicModelPdfTemplate
- `services/geminiService.ts` — browser fetch client to `/api/gemini/*`
- `services/fileService.ts` — document → images/markdown
- `services/pdfService.ts` — PDF/ZIP export
- `server.ts` + `server/geminiLogicModel.ts` — Gemini extract
- `constants.ts` — extraction prompt
- `types.ts` — LogicModel and processing types
- `docs/specs/` — PRD + living roadmap

## Architecture principles
- Up to two Gemini calls per multi-page document: an optional detect-logic-models pre-pass
  (`server/geminiLogicModelGroups.ts`, splits a document containing more than one logic model)
  followed by extract (`server/geminiLogicModel.ts`) — not single-pass (fixed 2026-09-19; see
  `docs/specs/multi-logic-model-pdf-v1.md`)
- Prefer vision/image conversion for layout fidelity; fall back to markdown text extraction
- Schema-constrained Gemini JSON matching `LogicModel` in `types.ts`
- Human-in-the-loop editing before export
- Vite proxies `/api` → `localhost:3011`

## Guardrails
- **Zero-dependency preference:** Use native APIs before proposing new npm packages. Pause and explain before any install.
- **No scope creep:** Do not add features without explicit product scoping. See `docs/specs/current-prd.md` and `docs/specs/roadmap.md`.
- **Secrets:** `GEMINI_API_KEY` only in `.env.local`, read by Express. Never Vite-define into the client.

